/corporate-announcements/other/)\n\n[![InvestyWise](https://www.investywise.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/Investywise-Logo-Formats_Symbol-Positive-copy.webp)](https://www.investywise.com/)[![InvestyWise](https://www.investywise.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/Investywise-Logo-Formats_Symbol-negative-B-copy.webp)](https://www.investywise.com/)\n\n## What are You Looking For?\n\nSearch\n\n- [Company Update](https://www.investywise.com/category/corporate-announcements/company-updates/)\n- [Board Meeting](https://www.investywise.com/category/corporate-announcements/board-meeting/)\n- [Company Results](https://www.investywise.com/category/corporate-announcements/company-results/)\n- [Other Announcements](https://www.investywise.com/category/corporate-announcements/other/)\n- [Insider Trading / SAST](https://www.investywise.com/category/corporate-announcements/insider-trading-sast/)\n- [Corporate Action](https://www.investywise.com/category/corporate-announcements/corporate-action/)\n\n[InvestyWise News](https://www.investywise.com/author/ainews786/)\n\nonJuly 29, 2026\n\n# Star Health and Allied Insurance Co. Ltd. Q1 FY27 Earnings Call Presentation\n\n- [Company Update](https://www.investywise.com/category/corporate-announcements/company-updates/)\n\n![](https://i0.wp.com/www.investywise.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/STARHEALTH_20260729_201414_68a3c826.png?resize=1200%2C675&ssl=1)\n\n3 min read\n\n[Share in Twitter](https://twitter.com/share?t=Star%20Health%20and%20Allied%20Insurance%20Co.%20Ltd.%20Q1%20FY27%20Earnings%20Call%20Presentation&url=https://www.investywise.com/star-health-and-allied-insurance-co-ltd-q1-fy27-earnings-call-presentation/ \"Share in Twitter\")[Share on Facebook](https://www.facebook.com/sharer.php?text=Star%20Health%20and%20Allied%20Insurance%20Co.%20Ltd.%20Q1%20FY27%20Earnings%20Call%20Presentation&u=https://www.investywise.com/star-health-and-allied-insurance-co-ltd-q1-fy27-earnings-call-presentation/ \"Share on Facebook\")[Share in Linkedin](https://www.linkedin.com/shareArticle?mini=true&url=https://www.investywise.com/star-health-and-allied-insurance-co-ltd-q1-fy27-earnings-call-presentation/ \"Share in Linkedin\")[Copy link](https://www.investywise.com/star-health-and-allied-insurance-co-ltd-q1-fy27-earnings-call-presentation/ \"Copy link\")\n\nStar Health and Allied Insurance Co. Ltd. announced its Q1 FY27 Earnings Call Presentation, covering the quarter ended June 30, 2026. The presentation details the company\u2019s financial performance, business landscape, and key strategic updates. Key highlights include **robust growth in Gross Written Premium**, improved underwriting results with a **97.0% CISR**, and strong customer centricity metrics such as a **102% persistency**. The company is focusing on sustainable profitable growth through disciplined portfolio management and technology-driven initiatives.\n\n## Star Health Announces Q1 FY27 Earnings Call Presentation\n\nStar Health and Allied Insurance Company Limited has released its presentation for the Earnings Call pertaining to the First Quarter (Q1) of the Financial Year 2027 (FY27), which concluded on **June 30, 2026**. This presentation was made available to investors and analysts on **Thursday, July 30, 2026**, at 8:30 AM IST.\n\n## Key Financial Performance Highlights\n\nThe presented financials for Q1 FY27 showcase significant progress. The **Combined Insurance Service Ratio (CISR) improved to 97.0%** from 98.7% in Q1 FY26. The **Underwriting Result saw a substantial increase to \u20b9111 crore**, up from \u20b916 crore in the previous year\u2019s quarter. Profit After Tax (PAT) for Q1 FY27 stood at **\u20b9550 crore**, marking a 25% year-on-year growth. Return on Equity (ROE) also demonstrated strong performance, reaching **22.3%** for Q1 FY27.\n\n## Progress on Key Business Metrics\n\nGross Premium has shown consistent growth, reaching **\u20b918,606 crore for FY26**, with a projected trajectory for Q1 FY27. The Underwriting Result has moved from a negative \u20b9151 crore in FY25 to a positive \u20b9198 crore in FY26 and further to **\u20b9111 crore in Q1 FY27**. Normalised Profit After Tax also reflects positive momentum, with **\u20b91,222 crore in FY26** and **\u20b9386 crore in Q1 FY27**.\n\n## Business Landscape: Building a Distribution Moat\n\nThe company\u2019s strategy revolves around building a compounding distribution moat. This is underpinned by a **largest agency-led health distribution network** built over two decades, a fast-growing Digital Direct-to-Customer (D2C) channel, and conscious risk-selection. The **Granular Distribution** strategy includes a large agency force of **8.5 Lakh agents**, with 20,000 additions in Q1 FY27. The **Scaling D2C Play** is a profitable, fast-growing proprietary channel. The **First-time Buyer Engine** shows a high new-to-insurance mix of **94%** in Q1 FY27. Furthermore, a **Deep pan-India Footprint** is evident, with non-metro geographies contributing over 60% of fresh business.\n\n## Capabilities: Technology-Driven Efficiency\n\nStar Health leverages technology across its value chain to enhance outcomes. This includes twenty years of proprietary data on a unified data layer with AI/ML at scale. The **Distribution App (ATOM Pro)** enhances efficiencies with smart quotes and always-on dashboards, while the customer app catalyzes engagement across wellness and service touchpoints. Claims processing efficiency is strengthened with an intelligence layer, including generative AI embedded in claims processing and AI-ML powered architecture for mitigation of Fraud, Waste and Abuse (FWA).\n\n## ESG Initiatives\n\nThe company\u2019s commitment to Environmental, Social, and Governance (ESG) principles is highlighted by an S&P Global CSA Score of **53 for FY25**. Key initiatives include advancements in **clean energy adoption**, e-waste recycling, and digital resource conservation. Socially, Star Health focuses on **100% employee coverage** under training programs, increased woman workforce representation (from 29% to 32%), and reduced employee attrition. Governance measures include reasonable assurance for core parameters and strengthened ESG governance.\n\n## CSR: Arogya Seva Kendra\n\nThe Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) arm, Arogya Seva Kendra, is actively operating in **9 States**, targeting outreach to over 1 million lives in underserved districts. Currently, there are **32 Operational Clinics**, which have facilitated **56,794 visits**. A total of **52,005 Medical Tests** have been conducted, and **1,921 Pneumococcal vaccinations** have been administered.\n\n**Source:** [BSE](https://www.bseindia.com/xml-data/corpfiling/AttachLive/08aadb82-4eee-4d94-b2c8-71bfa7283828.pdf)\n\n[InvestyWise News](https://www.investywise.com/author/ainews786/)\n\nonJuly 29, 2026\n\n- [Company Update](https://www.investywise.com/category/corporate-announcements/company-updates/)\n\nShare\n\n[Share in Twitter](https://twitter.com/share?t=Star%20Health%20and%20Allied%20Insurance%20Co.%20Ltd.%20Q1%20FY27%20Earnings%20Call%20Presentation&url=https://www.investywise.com/star-health-and-allied-insurance-co-ltd-q1-fy27-earnings-call-presentation/ \"Share in Twitter\")[Share on Facebook](https://www.facebook.com/sharer.php?text=Star%20Health%20and%20Allied%20Insurance%20Co.%20Ltd.%20Q1%20FY27%20Earnings%20Call%20Presentation&u=https://www.investywise.com/star-health-and-allied-insurance-co-ltd-q1-fy27-earnings-call-presentation/ \"Share on Facebook\")[Share in Linkedin](https://www.linkedin.com/shareArticle?mini=true&url=https://www.investywise.com/star-health-and-allied-insurance-co-ltd-q1-fy27-earnings-call-presentation/ \"Share in Linkedin\")[Copy link](https://www.investywise.com/star-health-and-allied-insurance-co-ltd-q1-fy27-earnings-call-presentation/ \"Copy link\")\n\n[Chalet Hotels Q1 FY27 Investor Presentation Highlights Robust Performance](https://www.investywise.com/chalet-hotels-q1-fy27-investor-presentation/ \"Chalet Hotels Q1 FY27 Investor Presentation Highlights Robust Performance\")\n\nPrevious Article\n\n## Chalet Hotels Q1 FY27 Investor Presentation Highlights Robust Performance\n\n[JSW Energy Limited O2 Renewable Energy XXIV Private Limited Secures \"CARE A; Stable\" Rating](https://www.investywise.com/jsw-energy-credit-rating-assigned/ \"JSW Energy Limited O2 Renewable Energy XXIV Private Limited Secures \\\"CARE A; Stable\\\" Rating\")\n\nNext Article\n\n## JSW Energy Limited O2 Renewable Energy XXIV Private Limited Secures \"CARE A; Stable\" Rating\n\n## Read Next\n\n- [Company Update](https://www.investywise.com/category/corporate-announcements/company-updates/)\n\n![](https://i0.wp.com/www.investywise.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/GRWRHITECH_20261026_170556_6e7c5ede.png?resize=400%2C225&ssl=1)\n\n[Garware Hi-Tech Films: Reports Record Q2 FY27 Revenue of \u20b9696 Crore](https://www.investywise.com/garware-hi-tech-films-q2-fy27-earnings-conference-call-transcript/ \"Garware Hi-Tech Films: Reports Record Q2 FY27 Revenue of \u20b9696 Crore\")\n\n[InvestyWise News](https://www.investywise.com/author/ainews786/)\n\nonOctober 26, 2026\n\n## [Garware Hi-Tech Films: Reports Record Q2 FY27 Revenue of \u20b9696 Crore](https://www.investywise.com/garware-hi-tech-films-q2-fy27-earnings-conference-call-transcript/)\n\nGarware Hi-Tech Films Limited announced a strong performance for the second quarter of FY27, achieving its highest-ever quarterly revenue of\u2026\n\n- [Company Update](https://www.investywise.com/category/corporate-announcements/company-updates/)\n\n![](https://i0.wp.com/www.investywise.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/TATACONSUM_20261026_170218_1f99ead3.png?resize=400%2C225&ssl=1)\n\n[Tata Consumer Products: Q2 FY27 Revenue Up 14%, EBITDA Grows 18%](https://www.investywise.com/tata-consumer-products-investor-presentation-on-unaudited-financial-results/ \"Tata Consumer Products: Q2 FY27 Revenue Up 14%, EBITDA Grows 18%\")\n\n[InvestyWise News](https://www.investywise.com/auth